THE FENCE. Roster grew 8 -> 9 with "FOUNDATION_PRELAUNCH_MISSION_GRAPH_MISMATCH" appended to FOUNDATION_PRELAUNCH_CODES. The comparison sits immediately after the `brief.ok` check and BEFORE `durableContext` / `produceLaunchTemplateFields`, so no template is built and discarded:

  if (brief.revisionId !== durable.record.graphRevisionRef
    || brief.graphContentHash !== durable.record.graphContentHash) {
    return refuse("FOUNDATION_PRELAUNCH_MISSION_GRAPH_MISMATCH", `the mission brief was read from graph ${brief.revisionId}/${brief.graphContentHash} but the sealed context is bound to ${durable.record.graphRevisionRef}/${durable.record.graphContentHash}`);
  }

RAILS HELD: compares the RE-READ `durable.record.*`, never the in-memory `provenance` (task rail 1); consumes only the traceable fields the producer already returns - NodeBriefRequest is untouched and no third graph read was added (task rail 2); `upstream` defaults to null so the code stays this layer's own and no producer refusal is flattened into it (task rail 3). A 6-line comment above the fence records WHY the window is real: the selection's horizon fence covers only its own read window, the brief is a second read taken outside it, the store is WAL-mode SQLite held open by other processes, and the failure mode is evidence attesting graph A's context digest while the agent worked graph B's instructions.

